implementationPlan.description:
Page half in moe-vscode/media/chat.js.

Add a local function deselectChannel() next to selectChannel. It must:
- set currentChannel = null, chatInput.disabled = true and sendBtn.disabled = true;
- restore the initial empty state with DOM calls only: messagesEl.textContent = '', then a createElement('div') with className 'empty-state' and textContent 'Select a channel to start chatting' (the text ChatViewProvider's HTML ships), appended with messagesEl.appendChild;
- call renderPins(), which hides the pinned section because pinCache[null] is empty;
- call saveState(), so a webview reload cannot restore the dead id.

In the 'updateChannels' case, after channels = data.channels || [] and before renderChannels(), call deselectChannel() when currentChannel is set and !channels.some(function(ch) { return ch.id === currentChannel; }). The existing auto-select branch (if (!currentChannel && channels.length > 0) selectChannel(channels[0].id)) then falls back to the first remaining channel. That is normally #general, because the daemon sorts channels by createdAt. The branch also posts selectChannel, so the extension loads that channel's messages and pins. A still-listed selection is left untouched.

No added line may contain a token from the project forbiddenPatterns rail: write markup only through textContent, createElement and appendChild.

Error handling: a missing channels array already degrades to [] and lands in the no-channel state instead of throwing.

Re-run `node --test moe-vscode/tests/wire-parity.test.cjs`: every row passes.

Adversarial self-review of this task's diff only: the two product files plus the new test.

(1) Mutation check, in a snapshot copy and never in the checkout (recipe in mem:gotcha-vscode-notifier-seam-and-link-injection). Each of these mutants must fail a wire-parity row by assertion, not by a harness error:
- drop the blank-reason guard;
- trim the reason;
- skip sendMessage's connected check;
- drop the unknown-id length guard;
- fire before the state write;
- drop the deselectChannel() call;
- drop saveState() or the disabled flags in deselectChannel.
(2) A duplicate CHANNEL_DELETED is a no-op.
(3) A still-listed selection never re-posts selectChannel.
(4) A malformed frame never throws.
(5) MoeDaemonClient.ts has no new import, and ChatViewProvider.ts and every existing test file are unchanged.
(6) Grep the added lines for every project forbiddenPatterns token. Look for a vacuous assertion, such as a stub that replaces the recorder instead of recording first.

Record the findings in the step note, and fix any real defect before complete_task.
